Short:        Text editor for programmers, with project tree and help
Author:       André Gewert <agewert@ubergeek.de>
Uploader:     André Gewert <agewert@ubergeek.de>
Type:         text/edit
Version:      1.0
Architecture: m68k-amigaos >= 3.2.0
Requires:     AmigaOS 3.2, dev/gui/html_gadget.lha (1.2, for the help)
Distribution: Aminet

TinyDev is a text editor for programmers on AmigaOS 3.2, built with
ReAction. It runs on a 68000, but is meant for 68030 to 68060 machines.

TinyDev
-------
 - several documents in tabs, each a texteditor.gadget: selection,
   clipboard, undo/redo, line numbers; LF, CR and CRLF line endings are
   kept; safe saves through a temporary file
 - syntax highlighting of C and AmigaDOS scripts
 - folder tree of the project (dirtree.gadget) that follows changes on
   disk, and a minimap (minimap.gadget)
 - find and replace in the document, in all open documents or in all
   files of the project, as plain text or with regular expressions
 - bookmarks, saved per project, with a bookmark list
 - toolbar with AISS images, images and text or text only
 - help pages in English and German, shown by the HelpViewer
 - settings saved as tool types of the TinyDev icon

HelpViewer
----------
Shows a drawer of HTML help pages with html.gadget: the pages by their
titles in a tree on the left, Back, Forward and Home. It runs on its
own, so TinyDev can be quit while the help stays open.

Installation
------------
TinyDev runs directly from the archive: it finds its classes, catalogs
and help pages next to it (Classes/, Catalogs/, Help/). html.gadget must
be installed in SYS:Classes/Gadgets/ or lie next to the HelpViewer.

Contents
--------
 TinyDev              the editor
 TinyDev-Scout        source analysis commodity (ARexx port TINYDEV_SCOUT)
 parsers/c_parser     the C parser of Scout
 HelpViewer           the help viewer
 Help/                help pages (english, deutsch)
 Classes/Gadgets/     dirtree.gadget and minimap.gadget
 Catalogs/            translations (German)
 Docs/                documentation (README.md)
 Icons/               the archive's icons as GlowIcons and NewIcons (and
                      scripts that put them in place)
 Source/              complete source code (C, cross compiled with
                      bebbo's amiga-gcc)

